  "rules": [
    "Only corruption and governance matters count: misuse of public money, tender fraud, bribery, and abuse of government power or office. Other criminal cases and court rulings (for example firearm, hate speech or incitement cases) are not part of the rating.",
    "Only formal, public-record matters count: court rulings, commissions of inquiry, SIU and Public Protector reports, parliamentary ethics findings, criminal charges and officially confirmed investigations. Media allegations alone do not.",
    "Only conduct while the person held a party or public office counts. Crimes from before someone entered politics are not included.",
    "People are innocent until proven guilty. Findings can be overturned, and the record will be updated when they are.",
    "A party with no record items is not certified clean. Parties that have governed longer and at a bigger scale have faced more scrutiny.",
    "News headlines are shown for context only. They never change a rating."
