      "status_type": "final",
      "title": "State Capture Commission findings",
      "person": "ANC as an organisation",
      "summary": "The Zondo Commission found that state capture took hold during the Zuma administration, that the ANC failed to act against it, and that the party's practice of cadre deployment to public posts was unconstitutional and unlawful.",
      "status": "Final reports delivered in 2022. Related prosecutions are ongoing.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "Zondo Commission (overview)",
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zondo_Commission"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "party": "anc",
      "date": "2021-09-29",
      "tier": "finding",
      "category": "corruption",
      "role": "senior",
      "status_type": "final",
      "title": "Digital Vibes health contract",
      "person": "Zweli Mkhize (then Minister of Health)",
      "summary": "An SIU report found Mkhize's conduct in approving a R150 million Department of Health contract to Digital Vibes, a company linked to his associates, was unlawful. He resigned as minister in August 2021.",
      "status": "SIU findings released in 2021. One former state employee was convicted in 2024.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "Daily Maverick, 29 Sep 2021",
          "url": "https://www.dailymaverick.co.za/article/2021-09-29-released-damning-siu-report-finds-at-least-r72m-fruitless-and-wasted-implicates-mkhize-doh-officials-in-digital-vibes-contract/"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "party": "anc",
      "date": "2026-05-08",
      "tier": "investigation",
      "category": "governance",
      "role": "leader",
      "status_type": "ongoing",
      "title": "Phala Phala impeachment inquiry",
      "person": "Cyril Ramaphosa (ANC president and President of South Africa)",
      "summary": "In 2022 an independent panel found there may be evidence of serious constitutional violations linked to the theft of foreign currency from the President's Phala Phala farm. Parliament voted not to act on it. In May 2026 the Constitutional Court ruled that vote unlawful, and Parliament has set up an impeachment inquiry.",
      "status": "Impeachment inquiry under way. No finding of guilt has been made.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "label": "EWN, 7 May 2026",
          "url": "https://www.ewn.co.za/2026/05/07/constitutional-court-ruling-could-reopen-ramaphosa-impeachment-process"
        },
